# The Kabyle preposition "deg" ("in") before a counted span gives a future
# offset.  Kabyle sentences on Tatoeba, with the English they are paired with:
#   8691123 "Ad d-nuɣal deg kraḍ n wayyuren."  -- "We'll be back in three months."
#   8691127 "Ad d-neqqel deg kraḍ n wayyuren." -- "We'll be back in three months."
#   8865882 "... ad awḍeɣ ɣer uɣerbaz ɣef uḍar deg 10 n tesdidin."
#           -- "I can walk to school in ten minutes."
deg
# "sya" ("from here, from now") before a counted span, Tatoeba 11266136
# "Ad teffeɣ tmacint sya tlata n dqayeq." -- "The train is leaving in three minutes."
sya
# Native answer, chronologia#1489 (comment 7218700864): "akka yiwen n wass" (in one day),
# "akka tlata n wussan" (in three days), "akka ṛebɛa n wussan" (in four days).
akka
